{
  "policy_prompt_for_action": "After the button had been pressed and the hand reopened at hover, several highlighted cubes remained uncompleted. The retained highlight frame identified them and completed_targets was empty, but the policy approached a highlighted blue cube rather than the recorded highlighted green cube. The rule allowing any uncompleted highlighted target therefore breaks SUFFICIENCY: it leaves different next waypoint positions equally eligible even though the available geometry can support a deterministic choice. Replace that unrestricted choice with this rule: when ready for lateral travel and not already hovering over an uncompleted highlighted cube, select the remaining highlighted cube with the smallest world x, meaning the cube nearest the robot along its forward axis; break an equal-x tie by increasing original world y. Apply this selection again after each completed cube has been returned and the open hand has retracted. Across the supplied multi-target trajectories, this selects green before red before blue in the three-target scene and green before blue in the two-target scene, without imposing a color priority. Retain the existing rule to descend when already approximately aligned over an uncompleted highlighted cube. Stable identity numbering remains independent of pickup priority, and completed identities remain excluded. Approach the selected cube at its calibrated center with z=0.15, fingers open, and the existing minimum-rotation square-edge-aligned yaw rule. No memory field or update condition needs to change: the retained highlight frame, completed identity set, and current geometry already supply the information required."
}

